This is just a curious question, but what version of the Wheaton Spoilers
are you referring to?  This sounds like an early revision to me.  The
last two versions have been rather un-vague.  In fact, we've tried to
give exact ranges or formulae wherever possible.

Also, the spoilers are a *heck* of a lot easier to read than the code, 
for the average player.  I know - I've read a lot of the code to create
sections of the spoilers.  Take for example any item or monster in the
game.  It's far simpler to look it up on a table with clearly marked column
headers than it is to take a bunch of comma delimited stuff, compare that
with a struct in a totally different file, check out what your DEFINE's
mean from yet another file, and then find out what they do in one more!

Anyways, enough defending the spoilers.  I think the file's popularity 
speaks for itself.  Oh - and no flame or other form of personal insult 
was intended!

